;; Stop-test regression (fidelity row SA11): the rewrite's right-hand side builds the
;; inner (Add a b) and the outer node flattens back onto the matched one, so the union
;; joins one class with itself and reported no change. The round minted (Add a b) and
;; the loop stopped before the second rule matched it: the check failed, naive and
;; semi-naive. Fixed by comparing the size stamp around the action phase.
(datatype E (Add E :assoc-comm) (G E) (a) (b) (c) (d))
(let t (Add (a) (b) (c)))
(rewrite (Add x y z) (Add (Add x y) z))
(rule ((Add x y)) ((union (G (Add x y)) (d))))
(run 10)
(check-eq (G (Add (a) (b))) (d))
